# ---------------- codebook.md ----------------
cb="# Codebook (40 codes, 7 groups, multi-label)\n\nBuilt bottom-up: embedding clusters + NMF topics (`data/processed/clusters_embedding.md`, `topics_nmf.md`) -> analyst (LLM) open coding of ~300 sampled documents -> 40 codes. A document can carry several codes. Document-level attributes: **stance** (E experience / Q question / A advice-to-others / O other) and **outcome** (S stopped / P paused / R reduced / C considering / K continuing / N none stated).\n\nPer-code columns: *n* = documents carrying the code in the final corpus (SIP-journey core, N=%d); *variant* = rule used by the final coder (regex | ml | and | or), picked by 5-fold OOF F1 on training labels; *holdout P/R* = precision/recall on the 150-document blind holdout, with support (gold positives) - **supports are small, treat as indicative**.\n\n"%H["N_core"]
for g,gn in GROUPS.items():
    cb+=f"## {g} - {gn}\n\n"
    for c,(grp,defn,rx) in CODES.items():
        if grp!=g: continue
        n=int(CF[CF.code==c].n_docs.iloc[0]); e=ens.loc[c]
        q=V[V.topic==c].head(2)
        cb+=f"### `{c}`\n- **Definition:** {defn}\n- **Docs coded:** {n} ({100*n/H['N_core']:.1f}% of journey-core) | **variant:** {thr['variant'][c]} | **holdout:** support {int(e.support_gold)}, P={e.precision:.2f}, R={e.recall:.2f}\n- **Regex rule:** `{rx[:400]}{'...' if len(rx)>400 else ''}`\n"
        for _,r in q.iterrows(): cb+=f"- **Exemplar ({r.source}{', '+str(r['product']) if isinstance(r['product'],str) else ''}):** \"{r.quote}\"  _(doc {r.doc_id})_\n"
        cb+="\n"
cb+="## Opportunity areas (groups of codes used in the scorecard)\n\n"+md(pd.DataFrame([dict(area=a,name=v["name"],codes=", ".join(v["codes"]),mechanism_rating_1to5=v["mech"],why=v["why"]) for a,v in AREAS.items()]))
cb+="\n**Revision note:** after the precision audit, `BH_FORGET` was removed from area A5 (audit precision 0/20: it mostly matched 'set and forget' advice) and A5 uses the regex-only `IA_ALERTS` rule (the AND-variant kept only 10 documents).\n"
open("codebook.md","w").write(cb)
